nd practices aimed at maintaining a healthy weight, particularly in the context of obesity. It refers to the process of adopting long-term lifestyle modifications to achieve and sustain a healthy weight. This encompasses various approaches, including dietary changes, physical activity, and behavioral adjustments, all designed to promote overall health and prevent weight-related issues.", "ENERGY INTAKE:Energy intake refers to the amount of calories consumed, which is crucial for managing diabetes and maintaining a healthy weight.", "AMERICAN COLLEGE OF ENDOCRINOLOGY:The American College of Endocrinology is a professional organization dedicated to the treatment and management of endocrine disorders, with a particular emphasis on obesity. It collaborates with the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists to develop and provide guidelines for effective obesity management, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest standards and practices in the field."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}